riking distance.", "watch": "Fresh independent polling or significant outside spending for Wellman could tighten the race, while Wagner's cash advantage could pull it further from the tossup range.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Ann Wagner (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Missouri's 2nd District leans Republican by about four points, and incumbent Ann Wagner is seeking re-election against Democratic nominee Fred Wellman and a Libertarian candidate. Wagner holds a large financial edge, with about $4.2 million on hand to Wellman's $242,000, and recent headlines highlight her work on rural health funding and bipartisan legislation.\n\nMost expert ratings place the seat at Likely Republican, with two raters at Lean Republican, one at Solid Republican, and one at Tossup. The only polls available are older, Democratic-sponsored surveys that showed a statistical tie, and prediction markets price Wagner's win chance near 70%. The forecast expects a Wagner win by mid-single digits, with Wellman competitive enough to keep the race on the board if the national environment breaks strongly for Democrats.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.2379, "margin": -4.26}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.2517, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.2424, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.2065, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.22, "margin": -4.5}]}